From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] QCLINUX: firmware: qcom_scm: enter EDL on "reboot edl"

"adb reboot edl" should drop the SoC into EDL / Sahara (9008) for reflashing.

The boot firmware (XBL/PBL + UEFI) enters EDL when bit 0 of the dload-mode
register is set on a cookie-retaining warm reset. That register is the one the
DT already describes as qcom,dload-mode = <&tcsr_2 0x13000> (absolute
0x01FD3000, == DloadCookieAddr in the platform XBL/UEFI). Two details matter:

  - The EDL cookie is bit 0. The existing "download mode" path sets bits [5:4]
    (QCOM_DLOAD_MASK, crashdump), which is a different function of the same
    register and does NOT enter EDL.
  - The cookie is only retained across a warm reset. The platform's warm reset
    is the Qualcomm SiP call 0xC3000922 (the same call the UEFI ResetSystemLib
    uses for EDL); architectural PSCI SYSTEM_RESET2 is not implemented under the
    Gunyah hypervisor and merely halts.

Register a restart handler (priority 192, above PSCI's 129) that, on reboot
reason "edl", sets the EDL cookie via the existing SCM IO write and issues the
SiP warm reset. It runs in machine_restart() (after device_shutdown(), so the
cookie survives the clean-reboot teardown); if the SiP call ever returns, the
lower-priority PSCI handler does a normal reset instead of hanging.

Other reboot reasons ("bootloader"/"recovery") are unaffected: those go through
the PMIC PON nvmem-reboot-mode.

Signed-off-by: Justinas Grauslis <justinas@8devices.com>
---
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include <linux/of_platform.h>
 #include <linux/of_reserved_mem.h>
 #include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/reboot.h>
 #include <linux/reset-controller.h>
 #include <linux/sizes.h>
 #include <linux/types.h>
@@ -539,6 +540,46 @@
 	return qcom_scm_io_writel(addr, new);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Reboot reason "edl" (e.g. "adb reboot edl"): drop into EDL / Sahara (9008).
+ *
+ * The boot firmware enters EDL when bit 0 of the dload-mode register
+ * (qcom,dload-mode, == DloadCookieAddr 0x01FD3000 in the XBL/UEFI) is set on a
+ * cookie-retaining warm reset. This is distinct from "download mode", which is
+ * bits [5:4] (crashdump) of the same register and is NOT EDL.
+ *
+ * The retaining warm reset is the Qualcomm SiP call 0xC3000922 (the same one
+ * the UEFI uses); unlike architectural PSCI SYSTEM_RESET2 it is honoured under
+ * the Gunyah hypervisor. Done from a restart handler (priority above PSCI's
+ * 129) so it runs after device_shutdown(); if the SiP call ever returns, we
+ * fall through to the normal PSCI reset rather than hang.
+ */
+#define QCOM_SCM_EDL_COOKIE	BIT(0)
+#define QCOM_SCM_WARM_RESET	0xc3000922
+
+static int qcom_scm_edl_restart_handler(struct notifier_block *nb,
+					unsigned long action, void *data)
+{
+	const char *cmd = data;
+	struct arm_smccc_res res;
+
+	if (!cmd || strcmp(cmd, "edl"))
+		return NOTIFY_DONE;
+
+	if (__scm->dload_mode_addr)
+		qcom_scm_io_rmw(__scm->dload_mode_addr, QCOM_SCM_EDL_COOKIE,
+				QCOM_SCM_EDL_COOKIE);
+
+	arm_smccc_smc(QCOM_SCM_WARM_RESET, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, &res);
+
+	return NOTIFY_DONE;
+}
+
+static struct notifier_block qcom_scm_edl_restart_nb = {
+	.notifier_call = qcom_scm_edl_restart_handler,
+	.priority = 192,
+};
+
 static void qcom_scm_set_download_mode(u32 dload_mode)
 {
 	int ret = 0;
@@ -2426,6 +2467,9 @@
 	 */
 	qcom_scm_set_download_mode(download_mode);
 
+	/* Allow "reboot edl" to drop into EDL via the dload-cookie + warm reset. */
+	register_restart_handler(&qcom_scm_edl_restart_nb);
+
 	/*
 	 * Disable SDI if indicated by DT that it is enabled by default.
 	 */
